// `try cast<T>(x)` yields `Optional<T>` and, like `try new`, reads that result type off the DECLARED
// destination. A local, an argument and a return type all supply one (try_cast_value_position); nested
// inside another expression there is nothing to read, and the diagnostic must name the two verbs that DO
// work in this position.
fn int32 main() {
    int32 v = 300;
    return cast<int32>(try cast<int8>(v));
}
